  "question": {
    "text": "A copper block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is heated to a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and is placed on a large ice block. What is the maximum amount of ice that can melt?<br />[Specific heat of copper : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>39</mn><msup><mi>Jg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mo>&#8728;</mo></mmultiscripts><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and latent heat of fusion of water : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>335</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Jg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
  },
